  "body": "Adds **Prism**, a standalone experimental Java 17 Tank Royale bot (`experiments/Prism/`) built from `docs/diamond-port-clean-room-specification.md`, with Facet renamed to Prism/`PRISM_*`. It is registered in stephanelee/robocode#104.\n\n**The single registered 200-round screen is queued after independent premeasurement review.** No outcome or strength claim is available yet.\n\n### What's included\n- **Bot:** engine boundary with one transaction per tick; engine-native predictor; waves with exact circular footprints; analytic, long-history, recent and melee-displacement guns with a frozen-prediction virtual selector; energy-ledger fire inference and forecast waves; two-wave/three-action surfing with learned danger, a flattener and bullet shadows; minimum-risk melee; decoupled radar; bounded stores with a 128 MiB guard. See `experiments/Prism/README.md`.\n- **Decision log:** `docs/prism-implementation-decisions.md`, with provenance, engine contracts and 24 documented assumptions or deviations.\n- **Protocol and harness:** `docs/prism-screen-protocol.md`, `docs/prism/screen-plan.json`, `tools/prism_screen.py`, `tools/PrismBattle.java`, and the manual workflow `prism-screen.yml` (defaults to check-only). The harness refuses to run without a recorded review URL and a matching JAR hash.\n- **CI:** `ci.yml` builds and tests Prism under Java 17 and verifies source/JAR parity. All jobs are pinned to `ubuntu-26.04`.\n\n### Evidence\n- **Real engine trace** (`experiments/Prism/fixtures/engine-trace-1`). Scripted probe bots ran in an isolated embedded-server 1.4.0 battle (never port 7654). Every non-collision transition matches `Physics.step` within 1e-6, including energy. Shots use the gun heading observed on the request tick and are confirmed one turn later. `Brain` infers exactly the mover's single power-1.0 shot and no false shots from repeated wall damage.\n- **Engine facts found by the trace:** target speed 0 stops instantly; the engine applies its wall constraint twice; a diagonal wall push pins the bot. Java 17 on Windows needs `-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8` for the descriptor's author name.\n- **Lifecycle smoke** (`fixtures/lifecycle-smoke-1`). Non-competitive: 3 rounds against a passive probe. 33/33 shots confirmed, 0 failures, **1 skipped turn in 566**, worst decision 102.8 ms.\n- **Tests:** 39/39 JUnit and 17/17 harness tests pass (Microsoft OpenJDK 17.0.18). Two clean builds produced byte-identical JARs.\n- **Hashes:** `Prism.jar` SHA-256 `8c045f80d37a3076ced7b337b020d14bf3942c6c2a89152f11021f8ff9e9e7ca`; source tree `experiments/Prism/src` = `7c3ce215060b47c9de0c53a89ce39ca96da62c6f`.\n\n### Provenance (please check)\n- Implemented from the specification, the official Tank Royale v1.4.0 source and API, and my own traces. No Diamond, Facet or other-bot implementation was opened.\n- The working clone was a partial (blob:none) sparse checkout excluding the restricted paths. **Incident:** a late `git ls-files --eol` lazily fetched 352 restricted-path blobs into the local object store. None were displayed or opened, and the clone should be deleted.\n- Disclosure: as a language model, my pretraining may include public Robocode code, possibly the original open-source Java Diamond. It was not consulted.\n\n### Limitations\n- Melee is validated only with synthetic fixtures, and no melee screen is registered, so this is a duel-first milestone, not completion of the full specification's validation.\n- The two-axis corner clamp is checked against the engine formula only.\n- Shadows are always capped at 75%.\n- Turn-budget compliance is not yet demonstrated in real matches.\n\nPlease do not merge without independent review. The implementer will not merge this PR.\n\n### Continuation status\n\nAll four gameplay and two clearance findings were verified fixed. After the zero-game manual-dispatch HTTP404, a label-trigger route and two concrete prelaunch opponent-staging fixes were independently reviewed. Final [full-acquisition clearance](https://github.com/stephanelee/robocode/pull/105#issuecomment-6635424606) binds code head `e4d51c5c32ab22bfcf93ecb5ce388dcd868c53ae`; approval-only execution head `0ac58d50ddaf041d0103a125b745fd4f2709a90c` changes only the two approval fields. The semantic/path guard passes. Earlier intermediate clearances were explicitly withdrawn before launch.\n\nThe sole `run-prism-screen-v1` label has started [run41863990617](https://github.com/stephanelee/robocode/actions/runs/41863990617), currently queued for its Ubuntu26.04 runner. Immediately before launch the receipt was absent and no earlier Prism screen run existed. The candidate source/JAR and registered13-game/200-round criteria/population are unchanged. No reruns, replacements, retuning or automatic confirmation. Branch writes are frozen through this attempt. I am the continuation implementer; final evidence/merge requires a separate independent agent. No parallel launch should be made.\n",
